{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0e091644-aa1f-42fe-b2a1-2ca972f5e406","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97d3456258611aa7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9007-_x1zvgsw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002.md","content":"# External vector store connection registration and Llama Stack RAG consumption\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the external-connection posture end to end on the Llama\nStack side: data scientists can register an external vector store connection\nper project with validated connectivity, and Llama Stack distributions in\nthat project consume the registered connection as the RAG vector provider\nwithout hand-editing distribution configs. It applies only if the\nexternal-connection-only posture is selected. Registration and consumption\nare bundled in one epic because they share the same connection contract and\nthe same owning team — splitting them would force two epics to build the\nsame data structure independently.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A per-project connection registration mechanism for external vector stores\n  (the connection contract: endpoint and credentials handling, project\n  scoping).\n- Connectivity validation performed at registration time, with clear\n  failure reporting.\n- Llama Stack distribution consumption of the registered connection as the\n  vector-RAG provider, following Llama Stack's provider-plugin configuration\n  model, with no hand-edited distribution configs.\n- Definition of which external vector store types are sanctioned/supported\n  for registration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Data scientists can register an external vector store connection per\n  project.\n- Registration validates connectivity to the external store and reports\n  failures clearly.\n- Llama Stack distributions in the project consume the registered connection\n  for RAG (vector insertion and retrieval) with no manual edits to\n  distribution configuration.\n- The set of supported external vector store types is defined and documented\n  (the strategy leaves this breadth undefined; the implementing team defines\n  it as part of this work).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0, external-connection variant): data scientists can register an\n  external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity.\n- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":53490,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b56f7aa1f4d5ba80","agent_id":"a782353020da01641","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"918bd584-cd70-4670-a98f-bdd56cd2f461","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:52:43.379Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007"}
