{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-803f5d361b441e7b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 1\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9007: Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads\n11\t\n12\t## Triage\n13\t\n14\tNot below threshold: although the strategy is compact, it contains a genuine,\n15\texplicitly-flagged open question — the first supported vector store posture\n16\t(platform-managed Milvus vs external-connection-only) is undecided, and the\n17\tstrategy itself states the answer \"forks the implementation structure for\n18\tHLR-2 through HLR-5\". The genuine-unknowns escape condition in Step 0\n19\tapplies, so the strategy received a full decomposition with a gating\n20\tInvestigation and conditional branches. Not documentation-only: code changes\n21\tare required in Llama Stack, Dashboard, and (on the managed path) the\n22\tPlatform Operator.\n23\t\n24\t## Approach\n25\t\n26\t- HLR-1 (the posture decision) is the gating Investigation (E001). It has\n27\t  exactly two bounded outcomes, so the decomposition uses conditional\n28\t  branches:\n29\t  - **Branch A — platform-managed**: operator-deployed Milvus with\n30\t    productized images (HLR-2, managed variant).\n31\t  - **Branch B — external-connection-only**: per-project external vector\n32\t    store connection registration with validated connectivity (HLR-2,\n33\t    external variant).\n34\t- All implementation work for HLR-2 through HLR-5 lives in the branches; the\n35\t  main plan consists of the Investigation alone.\n36\t- Milvus is a new component (no architecture context file, not in the\n37\t  canonical RHAI component list), so Branch A carries the standard onboarding\n38\t  chain: repo-onboarding + license-validation in parallel, konflux-onboarding\n39\t  after repo-onboarding, and the general implementation after\n40\t  license-validation and parallel with konflux-onboarding.\n41\t- The external path introduces no new platform component (customer-managed\n42\t  stores), so Branch B has no onboarding chain.\n43\t\n44\t## Epic List\n45\t\n46\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n47\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-E001 | Decide the first supported vector store posture (platform-managed vs external-connection-only) | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for Milvus | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux build-pipeline onboarding for the Milvus midstream repo | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005 | Platform Operator deployment and lifecycle for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack RAG provider consumption of the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E008 | Documentation for the platform-managed vector store posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 | External vector store connection registration and Llama Stack RAG consumption | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003 | Dashboard connection-management UI for external vector stores | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E004 | Documentation for the external-connection vector store posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n59\t\n60\t`epic_count=11` counts all epics including branches (1 main-plan + 10 branch\n61\tepics).\n62\t\n63\t## Dependency DAG\n64\t\n65\t```mermaid\n66\tgraph TD\n67\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: posture decision\"]\n68\t    E001 --> AE002[\"A-E002 repo-onboarding (Milvus)\"]\n69\t    E001 --> AE003[\"A-E003 license-validation (Milvus)\"]\n70\t    AE002 --> AE004[\"A-E004 konflux-onboarding (Milvus)\"]\n71\t    E001 --> AE005[\"A-E005 Platform Operator managed store\"]\n72\t    AE003 --> AE005\n73\t    AE005 --> AE006[\"A-E006 Llama Stack provider wiring\"]\n74\t    AE005 --> AE007[\"A-E007 Dashboard managed UI\"]\n75\t    AE002 --> AE008[\"A-E008 docs (managed)\"]\n76\t    AE003 --> AE008\n77\t    AE004 --> AE008\n78\t    AE005 --> AE008\n79\t    AE006 --> AE008\n80\t    AE007 --> AE008\n81\t    E001 --> BE002[\"B-E002 connection registration + consumption\"]\n82\t    BE002 --> BE003[\"B-E003 Dashboard connection UI\"]\n83\t    BE002 --> BE004[\"B-E004 docs (external)\"]\n84\t    BE003 --> BE004\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\tArrows point from dependency to dependent. Branch epics exist only if the\n88\tInvestigation selects that outcome; branch-internal edges apply within their\n89\tbranch. Every branch epic carries `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9007-E001` (also listed\n90\tin its `dependencies`) with `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` — if the other\n91\tposture is chosen, the branch is dropped in favor of its counterpart.\n92\t\n93\t## DAG Justification\n94\t\n95\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n96\t|------|------|-----------|\n97\t| E001 → every branch epic | Rule 3 | The posture decision determines existence and scope of all downstream work; every branch epic is a true gate (`remove`). Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional branches instead of phased decomposition. |\n98\t| A-E002 ∥ A-E003 (both from E001) | Rule 7 | repo-onboarding and license-validation take independent inputs and start in parallel. |\n99\t| A-E002 → A-E004 | Rule 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n100\t| A-E003 → A-E005 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial; a license failure changes the dependencies and the approach of the managed deployment. |\n101\t| A-E004 ∥ A-E005 (no edge either way) | Rules 10, 13 | Konflux config is independent of operator code, and the productized Milvus image digest is a configuration reference filled in at execution time — it is an acceptance-criteria gate (\"pinned image digest available\") on A-E005, never a DAG edge. |\n102\t| A-E002 ↛ A-E005 (no edge) | Rule 6 | repo-onboarding does not block other repos; the operator work lives in the Platform Operator repo, not the Milvus midstream repo. |\n103\t| A-E005 → A-E006 | Rules 12, 13 | The Llama Stack provider wiring builds against the operator-provided managed store capability (its deployment surface/endpoint). |\n104\t| A-E005 → A-E007 | Rules 12, 13 | The Dashboard UI reads and writes the operator's CRs for the managed store (Dashboard integrates via Kubernetes CRs per architecture context). |\n105\t| A-E006 ∥ A-E007 | Rule 14 | Different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n106\t| A-E002…A-E007 → A-E008 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by ALL Implementation epics of the branch (onboarding chain + feature epics); docs always last. |\n107\t| B-E002 → B-E003 | Rules 12, 13 | The Dashboard connection UI builds against the connection registration capability and its data structure. |\n108\t| B-E002, B-E003 → B-E004 | Rule 11 | docs blocked by all branch implementations. |\n109\t\n110\tNo onboarding chain on Branch B: no new platform component is introduced\n111\t(external stores are customer-managed), and both Llama Stack and Dashboard are\n112\texisting Konflux-onboarded components per architecture context.\n113\t\n114\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n115\t\n116\t| HLR | Priority | Branch A (platform-managed) | Branch B (external-connection-only) |\n117\t|-----|----------|------------------------------|-------------------------------------|\n118\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9007-E001 | RHAISTRAT-9007-E001 |\n119\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 |\n120\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002 |\n121\t| HLR-4 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E007 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003 |\n122\t| HLR-5 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E008 | RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E004 |\n123\t\n124\tFull coverage — no orphaned HLRs. Notes:\n125\t\n126\t- HLR-2 is branch-disjoint by construction; the strategy's Out of Scope\n127\t  explicitly excludes shipping both postures in the same release.\n128\t- On Branch B, HLR-2 and HLR-3 are bundled into a single epic: both land on\n129\t  Llama Stack (same component and team) and share the connection data\n130\t  structure — splitting would force two epics to build the same contract\n131\t  independently (Step 5 boundary rule). On Branch A they are separate epics\n132\t  because they belong to different components and teams (Platform Operator vs\n133\t  Llama Stack).\n134\t- HLR-5 is P2 in the strategy, but the docs epics take P1 via the\n135\t  docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major`\n136\t  → P1).\n137\t\n138\t## Component Mappings\n139\t\n140\t- **Milvus** is not in the canonical RHAI component list\n141\t  (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) and has no architecture context file. The\n142\t  Branch A onboarding epics are assigned to **Llama Stack**, its sponsoring\n143\t  component — the Llama Stack architecture context explicitly lists\n144\t  \"Milvus/vector providers for RAG workflows\" as a dependency — because no\n145\t  vector-store parent category exists in the canonical list.\n146\t- **Platform Operator** is a canonical Jira component but has no architecture\n147\t  context file — see Health Warnings.\n148\t\n149\t## Health Warnings\n150\t\n151\tNon-blocking; human verification recommended:\n152\t\n153\t1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table,\n154\t   no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, no\n155\t   Non-Functional Requirements, and no Staff Engineer Input. Team ownership\n156\t   was inferred from architecture context (RHOAI GenAI for Llama Stack,\n157\t   RHOAI Dashboard for Dashboard); \"RHOAI Platform Operator\" and\n158\t   \"RHOAI Documentation\" are placeholders pending confirmation.\n159\t2. **Platform Operator platform presence unverifiable.** The Platform\n160\t   Operator has no architecture context file, so its presence in the platform\n161\t   cannot be validated by the architecture-context rule. Because the strategy\n162\t   explicitly presumes it exists (\"deploy the managed vector store through\n163\t   the Platform Operator\"), it is treated as an existing component to modify\n164\t   rather than generating an onboarding chain. Flagged for human\n165\t   verification; if the operator genuinely needs onboarding, Branch A gains\n166\t   the standard chain.\n167\t3. **Undefined supported-store breadth on the external path.** The strategy\n168\t   does not enumerate which external vector store types are sanctioned.\n169\t   Captured as an acceptance criterion on BRANCH-B-E002 (the supported store\n170\t   types must be defined) rather than an Investigation — the answer does not\n171\t   change which epics exist or what they do.\n172\t4. **Docs priority note.** HLR-5 (P2) maps to docs epics at P1 via the\n173\t   docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority Major → P1). Not an\n174\t   inversion, but reviewers should be aware docs are prioritized from\n175\t   strategy-level priority, not HLR-5's P2.\n176\t\n177\t## Tiered Delivery\n178\t\n179\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing — the\n180\tfork is an internal product decision resolved by the gating Investigation,\n181\tand the strategy explicitly rules out shipping both postures in one release.\n182\tEach branch is a complete plan for its outcome.\n183\t\n184\t## Branch Mechanics\n185\t\n186\tBranch files use the `-BRANCH-<letter>-` filename convention. Each sets\n187\t`branch=<letter>`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9007-E001` (also present in its\n188\t`dependencies`), and `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` with a fallback\n189\tapproach describing the counterpart branch. Main-plan epics declare no\n190\tdependencies on branch epics. Branch epics are excluded from the main-plan\n191\tcritical path (`critical_path_length=1`); the longest branch-internal chain\n192\tis 5 (E001 → A-E003 → A-E005 → A-E006 → A-E008).\n193\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82de540447b0cce7","agent_id":"a313bdc5523438bd1","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"2c4909a4-841f-42a4-9219-2c1f53f8d59a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:57:36.740Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-803f5d361b441e7b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
