{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b42db1960072790d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Decide the first supported vector store posture: platform-managed vs external-connection-only'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide the first supported vector store posture: platform-managed vs external-connection-only\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's gating open question: which vector store\n30\tposture the platform productizes first — a platform-managed vector database\n31\t(operator-deployed Milvus with productized images and lifecycle) or an\n32\texternal-connection-only posture (a sanctioned way for data scientists to\n33\tregister customer-managed vector stores per project). The outcome determines\n34\tthe existence and shape of every downstream implementation epic in this\n35\tstrategy, so it must be decided and documented before any implementation\n36\twork starts.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Produce a documented evaluation comparing both postures against the\n41\t  criteria named in the strategy: supportability cost, disconnected-environment\n42\t  viability, and time-to-market.\n43\t- Assess the platform-managed path: what productizing Milvus entails\n44\t  (midstream repository, productized images, lifecycle through the Platform\n45\t  Operator) and its ongoing support burden.\n46\t- Assess the external-connection p