ion configs is required.\n51\t- Validate RAG workflows end-to-end against the managed store.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A Llama Stack distribution uses the managed vector store for RAG (vector\n56\t  insertion and retrieval) with no manual edits to distribution\n57\t  configuration.\n58\t- Provider configuration for the managed store is derived from the platform\n59\t  deployment rather than hand-edited per distribution.\n60\t- An end-to-end RAG workflow is validated against the managed store.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n65\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82de540447b0cce7","agent_id":"a313bdc5523438bd1","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"029b6d2e-0b91-40b5-8856-7bc2dcb4c817","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:58:03.006Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb98dac770e2b48d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
