{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b09d88db50a78d89","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002\n3\ttitle: External vector store connection registration and Llama Stack RAG consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the platform-managed posture is selected, external connection\n16\t    registration is not built; this epic is dropped and the platform-managed branch\n17\t    applies instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# External vector store connection registration and Llama Stack RAG consumption\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the external-connection posture end to end on the Llama\n39\tStack side: data scientists can register an external vector store connection\n40\tper project with validated connectivity, and Llama Stack distributions in\n41\tthat project consume the registered connection as the RAG vector provider\n42\twithout hand-editing distribution configs. It applies only if the\n43\texternal-connection-only posture is selected. Registration and consumption\n44\tare bundled in one epic because they share the same connection contract and\n45\tthe same owning team — splitting them would force two epics to build the\n46\tsame data structure independently.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- A per-project connection registration mechanism for external vector stores\n51\t  (the connection contract: endpoint and credentials handling, project\n52\t  scoping).\n53\t- Connectivity validation performed at registration time, with clear\n54\t  failure reporting.\n55\t- Llama Stack distribution consumption of the registered connection as the\n56\t  vector-RAG provider, following Llama Stack's provider-plugin configuration\n57\t  model, with no hand-edited distribution configs.\n58\t- Definition of which external vector store types are sanctioned/supported\n59\t  for registration.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Data scientists can register an external vector store connection per\n64\t  project.\n65\t- Registration validates connectivity to the external store and reports\n66\t  failures clearly.\n67\t- Llama Stack distributions in the project consume the registered connection\n68\t  for RAG (vector insertion and retrieval) with no manual edits to\n69\t  distribution configuration.\n70\t- The set of supported external vector store types is defined and documented\n71\t  (the strategy leaves this breadth undefined; the implementing team defines\n72\t  it as part of this work).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0, external-connection variant): data scientists can register an\n77\t  external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity.\n78\t- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n79\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82de540447b0cce7","agent_id":"a313bdc5523438bd1","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"69cde79a-a9e2-417b-b0b3-cd2f557c6634","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:58:09.604Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b09d88db50a78d89","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
