h defaults configured via the Dashboard's\n52\t  configuration conventions.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Data scientists can create, edit, and delete external vector store\n57\t  connections from the Dashboard.\n58\t- Connectivity test results from registration/validation are surfaced in the\n59\t  UI.\n60\t- The integration is behind a feature flag consistent with the Dashboard's\n61\t  configuration conventions.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-4 (P1): the Dashboard exposes the chosen integration — connection\n66\t  management UI for the external path.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82de540447b0cce7","agent_id":"a313bdc5523438bd1","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"55e2df9e-d14c-41db-9f9e-144a2799da0f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:58:10.907Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b4dbf9b5088c8ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
