{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11aac476c9fbc45","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9007\n10\t\n11\t## Review Summary\n12\t\n13\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n14\tRecommendation: accept\n15\t\n16\tReviewed against the strategy (artifacts/strat-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9007.md), the\n17\tdecomposition summary, all 11 epic files (1 main-plan + 7 Branch A + 3 Branch B),\n18\tall 11 AI signal rationale files, and the provisioned architecture context\n19\t(.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/ contains only\n20\tllama-stack.md and dashboard.md; .context/rhai-components.txt lists Platform\n21\tOperator but not Milvus).\n22\t\n23\t## Criterion Details\n24\t\n25\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n26\tTraceability matrix present and complete. All five HLRs map to epics in both\n27\tbranches: HLR-1 → E001; HLR-2 → A-E005 / B-E002; HLR-3 → A-E006 / B-E002;\n28\tHLR-4 → A-E007 / B-E003; HLR-5 → A-E008 / B-E004. Priority inheritance is\n29\tcorrect: the gating Investigation E001 is P0; every P0-work prerequisite\n30\t(A-E002/E003/E004/E005, B-E002) is P0; P1 epics (A-E006/E007, B-E003) are\n31\tenabled by P0 epics. The docs epics take P1 via the docs-authoring priority\n32\texception (strategy priority Major → P1), correctly applied and explicitly\n33\tdocumented in the summary. The B-E002 bundle of HLR-2 (P0) and HLR-3 (P1) was\n34\texamined for priority collapse and rejected as a violation: on the external\n35\tpath both HLRs land on the same component/team and share one connection\n36\tcontract — consumption is the completion of the registration capability, not a\n37\tdistinct deferrable feature, and Branch A splits them only because they belong\n38\tto different components there. Onboarding epics correctly report themselves as\n39\tprovisioning prerequisites in HLR Traceability.\n40\t\n41\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n42\tDiagram and frontmatter cross-check: every arrow in the mermaid diagram\n43\t(E001→AE002, E001→AE003, AE002→AE004, E001→AE005, AE003→AE005, AE005→AE006,\n44\tAE005→AE007, AE002…AE007→AE008, E001→BE002, BE002→BE003, BE002/BE003→BE004)\n45\thas a matching entry in the target epic's dependencies, and every frontmatter\n46\tdependency appears in the diagram — no mismatches, no dangling references, no\n47\tcycles. Arrows point dependency → dependent per convention. Implementation-type\n48\tparallelism verified for every pair: no license-validation → repo-onboarding\n49\tedge (rule 7), no license-validation → konflux-onboarding edge (rule 8), and no\n50\tedge in either direction between konflux-onboarding A-E004 and any general\n51\timplementation epic (A-E005, A-E006, A-E007, B-E002, B-E003) (rule 10). The\n52\tMilvus image digest coupling between A-E004 and A-E005 is correctly handled as\n53\ta Rule 13 configuration reference — an acceptance criterion on A-E005 (\"pinned\n54\tdigest available from the build pipeline\"), not a dependencies edge. Branch\n55\tmechanics: all 10 branch files set branch (A/B, matching filename) and\n56\tgated_by=RHAISTRAT-9007-E001, which is also in each direct dependencies list;\n57\tno main-plan epic depends on a branch epic (E001 has no dependencies). No\n58\tuncaptured data/artifact dependencies found in epic content (A-E006/A-E007\n59\tconsume A-E005's CRs/endpoint via edges; B-E003 consumes B-E002's connection\n60\tcontract via edge). Critical path: main plan is 1 by design (branches are\n61\tconditional); longest branch-internal chain is 5, within the M-with-new-\n62\tcomponent heuristic (4-5). Rule 11 edges into the docs epics are present and\n63\tnot counted as serialization.\n64\t\n65\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n66\tEvery epic carries a single component/team tuple; no epic spans multiple teams.\n67\tThe Milvus onboarding chain is assigned to Llama Stack / RHOAI GenAI as the\n68\tsponsoring component, with explicit justification (Milvus is absent from the\n69\tcanonical component list; Llama Stack architecture context lists\n70\t\"Milvus/vector providers for RAG workflows\" — verified in\n71\trhoai-3.0/llama-stack.md). No scope duplication across sibling epics: A-E006\n72\tand B-E002 both wire Llama Stack provider consumption, but they live in\n73\tmutually exclusive conditional branches, not co-existing siblings; within each\n74\tbranch the operator (A-E005), Dashboard (A-E007), and Llama Stack (A-E006)\n75\tsurfaces are cleanly disjoint. Work-product types are not mixed: both docs\n76\tepics (A-E008, B-E004) are pure docs-authoring, separate from code epics. No\n77\tepic appears oversized; B-E002 is the largest (registration + validation +\n78\tconsumption + sanctioned-type definition) but is one logical change on one\n79\tcomponent with a shared contract, plausibly a single sprint.\n80\t\n81\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n82\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (managed vs external posture)\n83\tdetermines the existence of all downstream epics — it forks the plan, exactly\n84\tthe misclassification test's positive case. All ten branch epics are\n85\tImplementations producing concrete artifacts (repository, clearance record,\n86\tbuild pipeline, operator capability, provider wiring, UI, published docs).\n87\tGating metadata is complete and correct on every branch epic: gated_by is set,\n88\tgate_failure_impact has action=remove with a populated fallback_approach\n89\tdescribing the counterpart branch, and the gated_by target (E001) appears in\n90\teach epic's direct dependencies. Every epic listing the Investigation in\n91\tdependencies has gated_by set. E001 itself correctly has gated_by null. The\n92\tgates are true gates, not scheduling dependencies — the outcome removes the\n93\tentire branch.\n94\t\n95\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n96\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries investigation_signals\n97\t(ai_signals null); all Implementation epics carry ai_signals\n98\t(investigation_signals null); no cross-type contamination. All 11 ai-signals\n99\trationale files exist and their values match frontmatter exactly. E001's\n100\tsignals are consistent with the rubric: question_specificity +1 (concrete,\n101\tenumerable question with named criteria), source_accessibility 0 (the answer\n102\tis a pending product decision — correctly not marked 1), human_judgment_required\n103\t-2 (stakeholder sign-off decision). Signal values engage honestly with the\n104\tarchitecture context: A-E005 scores repo_access 0 and architecture_claims -1\n105\tbecause the Platform Operator has no architecture context file (verified —\n106\tonly llama-stack.md and dashboard.md exist), matching the health warning;\n107\tA-E006/A-E007/B-E002/B-E003 score architecture_claims +1 backed by verifiable\n108\tcontext (provider-plugin model, CR-based Dashboard integration,\n109\tOdhDashboardConfig feature flags). B-E002's open_questions +1 is justified: the\n110\tundefined supported-store breadth is captured as an acceptance criterion and\n111\tdoes not change the epic's scope or existence.\n112\t\n113\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n114\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy. Rule-\n115\tmandated ACs verified on every applicable epic: A-E004 has the Konflux\n116\tbuild-pipeline-green AC; A-E005 carries both the pinned-digest availability AC\n117\tand a platform build-green AC; both docs epics (A-E008, B-E004) have the\n118\ttechnical-review AC; both Dashboard epics (A-E007, B-E003) have feature-flag\n119\tACs consistent with the Dashboard's conventions; A-E005 covers lifecycle\n120\t(upgrade/scale/removal) and rollback behavior for the managed service. No epic\n121\tbody references sibling epics by bare draft ID — grepped all bodies; only full\n122\tepic IDs appear, and only in frontmatter.\n123\t\n124\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n125\tAll strategy scope is covered: the two-camp problem statement motivates both\n126\tbranch variants of HLR-2; all HLRs map in both branches; the Out of Scope\n127\tconstraints are respected (no both-postures epic, no embedding-model work).\n128\tThe conditional branches cover exactly the two bounded outcomes named in the\n129\tstrategy's open question, and the strategy's evaluation criteria\n130\t(supportability cost, disconnected-environment viability, time-to-market) are\n131\tcarried into E001's scope and ACs, with disconnected-environment behavior also\n132\tdocumented as a limit in A-E008. All three affected components (Llama Stack,\n133\tDashboard, Platform Operator) have corresponding epics. Cross-epic consistency\n134\tholds: every item of E001's decision feeds a branch, and no branch silently\n135\tdrops a piece of the strategy's scope. Strategy-level gaps (missing Impacted\n136\tTeams, Dependencies, GWC ACs, NFRs, Staff Engineer Input sections) are\n137\texplicitly flagged as health warnings with the inferences made, not silently\n138\tdropped. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section, so no\n139\tDocumentation Support requirement is unmet — and docs epics exist anyway for\n140\tHLR-5.\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d71044d0af70a5c","agent_id":"a6ca1a39a804d0d7b","session_id":"1cf9837f-a22c-4111-9c91-090881190567","uuid":"f7568f24-a131-4ab8-a853-a4753b08685b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:03:01.018Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11aac476c9fbc45","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
